<body style="height: auto; min-height: auto;">Ref: {{{Case.Case_Number__c}}}<br />
<br />
Hi {{{Case.First_Name__c}}},
<p>Thank you for contacting the Qantas Customer Care team.<br />
<br />
I was sorry to hear your baggage was <em><strong>&lt;damaged/delayed/lost&gt;</strong></em> while travelling to {{{Case.Arrival_Airport__c}}}.<br />
<br />
<strong>Why was my bag lost/not loaded?</strong><br />
Baggage can be delayed for multiple reasons such as, operational issues, weight and balance requirements, weather, enhanced security checks or Airport infrastructure.&nbsp; Due to these complexities, we have not been able to pinpoint the specific reason in your case.<br />
<br />
<strong>Flights with other airlines</strong><br />
As this final flight was operated by {{{Case.Airline__c}}}, you'll need to lodge a report directly with them, and they'll process the claim for you.<br />
<br />
The airline that carries you to your final destination manages any baggage claim, ensuring the swift recovery of your belongings, without the need for multiple airlines to handle them.</p>

<p><strong>Next Steps</strong><br />
Please contact {{{Case.Airline__c}}} and their staff will be happy to help you with your claim.<br />
<br />
<strong>We're here to help</strong><br />
For more information about baggage that has been delayed, damaged or lost, head to <a href="https://www.qantas.com/au/en/travel-info/baggage/baggage-services.html#damaged-checked-baggage">Baggage Services</a>&nbsp;on our website.<br />
<br />
If you have any other questions in the meantime regarding a Qantas flight, don't hesitate to get in touch.</p>
